{
  "name": "cloud_underlight_layer_survey",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "SURVEY ONLY, no pins: locates \u00a723b's glow window on this tile before the real scenario pins anything in it. Every Probe here carries a dummy expectation and a huge tolerance, so the scenario passes regardless and the numbers are read out of the report's ActualValue fields \u2014 the parent CLAUDE.md's 'survey with sun_elevation before you pick an hour' note, run as a scenario. Latitude 45, day 40, the tile/season \u00a723's own scenario already established civil dusk on. \u00a723b's window is far narrower than \u00a723's: it runs from the horizon only down to the deck's shadow entry (~2.03\u00b0 for Overcast's 4000 m), which is a handful of minutes, so an hourly grid would miss it entirely. The Clear-weather block forces \u00a722's cloud fraction to a fixed 0.35 (see CloudCoverFractionOverride) because the live value depends on which absolute year the fixture booted into.",
